Armed with this observation, we present Self-Supervised Prompting (SSP) -- a novel ICL framework for 0-CLT to LRLs. Since the target LRL training data is not available in 0-CLT, SSP operates in two stages. In Stage I, SSP labels all test instances of LRL using training data from MRL. This may be done by LLM prompting (as in the experiment above), or using any other existing approaches for 0-CLT, such as by fine-tuning or adapters. Once (noisy) labels on target LRL are obtained, in Stage II, SSP uses ICL using these noisy test data points (except itself) as exemplars for further performance improvement.
